# Ripple conventions

## Shipping JS

- After changing `main.js`, bump the cache query in `index.html` (`main.js?v=YYYYMMDDxx`).
- Keep gameplay in `main.js` unless there is a clear reason to split.

## User-facing text

- Plain language only in UI, hints, registry blurbs, and in-pond messages.
- No em dashes or en dashes.
- No shell commands, file paths, or code blocks in product UI copy.

## Docs and git hygiene

- Do not commit or push personal `docs/ripple-user-guide.*` / `docs/Ripple-User-Guide.pdf`.
- Do not add AI "next steps" or assistant feedback voice into files meant for public readers.
- Prefer updating `.cursor/rules/` or `AGENTS.md` when you learn durable project facts other agents will need.

## Motion

Follow `.cursor/rules/natural-motion.mdc` for all creature and finale movement.
